            "normalized_html": "<p>We are given the equation <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\dfrac{5}{8}y - \\dfrac{2}{8}y = 6]</span> and are asked to solve for <span class=\"math\">[MATH: y.]</span></p><p>First, we simplify the left-hand side by combining like terms:\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: (5)/(8)y \u2212 (2)/(8)y|= ((5)/(8) \u2212 (2)/(8))y; = (3)/(8)y]</span></p><p>So, the equation becomes\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: (3)/(8)y|= 6.]</span></p><p>Now, we solve for <span class=\"math\">[MATH: y]</span> by multiplying both sides of the equation by <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\dfrac{8}{3}]</span>:\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: y|= 6 \u22c5 (8)/(3); = 16]</span></p><p>So, the value of <span class=\"math\">[MATH: y]</span> that satisfies the equation is <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 16.]</span></p>",
