    "readable_text": "Item 1 \u2014 Tutorial: Introduction\n\nContent:\nIn this topic, we'll practice solving linear equations with fractional coefficients.\n\n---\n\nItem 2 \u2014 Example: Solving Equations With Fractional Coefficients\n\nExample Prompt:\n[MATH: \\dfrac{2v}{5} = 14]\nIn the equation above, what is the value of [MATH: v?]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nWe are given the equation [MATH: \\dfrac{2v}{5} = 14] and are asked to solve for [MATH: v.]\n\nLet's solve the equation for [MATH: v{:}]\n\n[MATH: (2v)/(5)|= 14; 2v|= 14 \u22c5 5; 2v|= 70; v|= (70)/(2); v|= 35]\n\nSo, the value of [MATH: v] that satisfies the equation is [MATH: 35.]\n\n---\n\nItem 3 \u2014 Question 1\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: (3y)/(4) = 18]\nIn the equation above, what is the value of [MATH: y?]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 12]\nb. [MATH: 24]\nc. [MATH: 18]\nd. [MATH: 21]\ne. [MATH: 16]\n\n---\n\nItem 4 \u2014 Question 2\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: (2v)/(5) = 14]\nIn the equation above, what is the value of [MATH: v?]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 28]\nb. [MATH: 35]\nc. [MATH: 30]\nd. [MATH: 32]\ne. [MATH: 40]\n\n---\n\nItem 5 \u2014 Example: Solving Equations With Fractional Coefficients and Evaluating an Expression\n\nExample Prompt:\nCalculate [MATH: 8x] given that [MATH: \\dfrac{5}{8}x - 1 = 9.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nWe are given the equation [MATH: \\dfrac{5}{8}x - 1 = 9] and are asked to find the value of [MATH: 8x.]\n\nFirst, we solve the equation for [MATH: x{:}]\n[MATH: (5)/(8)x \u2212 1|= 9; (5)/(8)x|= 9 + 1; (5)/(8)x|= 10; 5x|= 80; x|= (80)/(5); x|= 16]\n\nNow, we substitute [MATH: x = 16] into [MATH: 8x{:}]\n[MATH: 8x|= 8 \u22c5 16; = 128]\n\n---\n\nItem 6 \u2014 Question 3\n\nPrompt:\nIf [MATH: (3)/(7)x \u2212 4 = 11,] then [MATH: 7x =][FREE_ENTRY 1].\n\n---\n\nItem 7 \u2014 Question 4\n\nPrompt:\nIf [MATH: (5)/(8)y \u2212 (2)/(8)y = 6,] what is the value of [MATH: y?]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 14]\nb. [MATH: 16]\nc. [MATH: 12]\nd. [MATH: 8]\ne. [MATH: 10]\n\n---\n\nItem 8 \u2014 Example: Solving Equations With Multiple Fractional Coefficients\n\nExample Prompt:\nIf [MATH: \\dfrac{5}{8}y - \\dfrac{2}{8}y = 6,] what is the value of [MATH: y?]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nWe are given the equation [MATH: \\dfrac{5}{8}y - \\dfrac{2}{8}y = 6] and are asked to solve for [MATH: y.]\n\nFirst, we simplify the left-hand side by combining like terms:\n[MATH: (5)/(8)y \u2212 (2)/(8)y|= ((5)/(8) \u2212 (2)/(8))y; = (3)/(8)y]\n\nSo, the equation becomes\n[MATH: (3)/(8)y|= 6.]\n\nNow, we solve for [MATH: y] by multiplying both sides of the equation by [MATH: \\dfrac{8}{3}]:\n[MATH: y|= 6 \u22c5 (8)/(3); = 16]\n\nSo, the value of [MATH: y] that satisfies the equation is [MATH: 16.]\n\n---\n\nItem 9 \u2014 Question 5\n\nPrompt:\nIf [MATH: (3)/(4)x \u2212 (1)/(2)x = 2,] what is the value of [MATH: x?]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 8]\nb. [MATH: 6]\nc. [MATH: 2]\nd. [MATH: 4]\ne. [MATH: 1]\n\n---\n\nItem 10 \u2014 Question 6\n\nPrompt:\nIf [MATH: (5)/(8)x \u2212 1 = 9,] then [MATH: 8x =][FREE_ENTRY 1]."
